Cheaper per call, more expensive when the model reconstructs something wrong three turns later.

The lever that actually holds quality is keeping the durable facts out of the chat entirely and pulling only the relevant, current ones back in per turn. I keep those facts as versioned markdown and retrieve them through `ctx` (`npx @promptowl/contextnest-cli`): local-first, each fact carries its history, and retrieval serves the current version instead of every match. Token cost tracks what you actually pull, not the size of the whole history. It’s MCP, so you can route cheap-vs-capable models without re-feeding context each time.

