    	ret
    
    oexRGBASetAlpha	ENDP`

Formats like GIF/PNG/WEBP have rgb + alpha channels… You can run a mask over it or just convert every pixel…

Generally RGBA is 4 bytes (1 per ‘color’) and then the image is further compressed ie with gzip similar algo…

* * *

> OpenAI may use a different method to generate the image (e.g. diffusion and segmentation), but when exported with transparency it’s still stored as standard RGBA with an 8-bit alpha channel — the same underlying format as any other PNG/WEBP.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
